  "claim": "Alison Nicole Mosshart was part of more rock music bands than the singer of \"I Want You So Bad\".",
  "evidencia": "Page: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: Alison Nicole Mosshart (born November 23, 1978) is an American singer, songwriter, artist, and occasional model best known as the lead vocalist for the indie rock band The Kills and blues rock band The Dead Weather.\nPage: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: She started her musical career in 1995 with the Florida punk rock band Discount which disbanded in 2000.\nPage: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: She then co-founded The Kills with British guitarist Jamie Hince (formerly of Scarfo and Blyth Power) in 2000 in London.\nPage: Ann Wilson. Sentence: Ann Dustin Wilson (born June 19, 1950) is an American musician, best known as the lead singer and songwriter of the hard rock band Heart.\nPage: I Want You So Bad. Sentence: The track is a ballad sung by Ann Wilson, and was released in a remixed form as the fourth and final single from Heart's ninth studio album, \"Bad Animals\", as well as being the band's final single of the 1980s.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: Alison Nicole Mosshart (born November 23, 1978) is an American singer, songwriter, artist, and occasional model best known as the lead vocalist for the indie rock band The Kills and blues rock band The Dead Weather.\nPage: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: She started her musical career in 1995 with the Florida punk rock band Discount which disbanded in 2000.\nPage: Alison Mosshart. Sentence: She then co-founded The Kills with British guitarist Jamie Hince (formerly of Scarfo and Blyth Power) in 2000 in London.\nPage: Ann Wilson. Sentence: Ann Dustin Wilson (born June 19, 1950) is an American musician, best known as the lead singer and songwriter of the hard rock band Heart.\nPage: I Want You So Bad. Sentence: The track is a ballad sung by Ann Wilson, and was released in a remixed form as the fourth and final single from Heart's ninth studio album, \"Bad Animals\", as well as being the band's final single of the 1980s.",
