        "original_id": "ae611280-c1c1-55c2-976e-1fdcae74548c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alison Mosshart, Jamie Hince, Ann Wilson\n- Bands: Discount, The Kills, The Dead Weather, Heart, Scarfo, Blyth Power\n- Songs and Albums: “I Want You So Bad”, Bad Animals\n- Roles: singers, songwriters, guitarist, artist, model\n\nFacts:\n- Ann Dustin Wilson was born on June 19, 1950, and she is an American musician best known as the lead singer and songwriter of the hard rock band Heart.\n- Alison Nicole Mosshart was born on November 23, 1978, and she is an American singer, songwriter, artist, and occasional model best known as the lead vocalist for The Kills and The Dead Weather.\n- Alison Mosshart started her musical career in 1995 with the Florida punk rock band Discount.\n- Discount disbanded in 2000.\n- In 2000, Alison Mosshart co-founded The Kills in London with British guitarist Jamie Hince.\n- Jamie Hince had previously been a member of Scarfo and Blyth Power.\n- “I Want You So Bad” is a ballad sung by Ann Wilson.\n- “I Want You So Bad” was released in remixed form as the fourth and final single from Heart’s ninth studio album Bad Animals, and it was Heart’s final single of the 1980s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
